# CocEnglish line-ending policy.
#
# Tooling parses committed documents byte-for-byte, so a CRLF working tree breaks
# gates on Windows even though CI (Linux) stays green:
#   - appwrite/scripts/schema-lib.mjs derives the 62-table declaration from
#     docs/data/DATA_MODEL.md and docs/data/PERMISSIONS.md with `$`-anchored
#     regexes; a trailing \r makes every table row fail to match.
#   - tools/audit/endpoint-matrix.mjs and tools/blueprint/generate-dart-contracts.mjs
#     hash generated output against the committed file.
# The extensions below are therefore checked out with LF, matching .editorconfig.
#
# Deliberately NOT a blanket `* text=auto eol=lf`: some tracked blobs were
# committed with CRLF (a few iOS asset manifests, analysis_options.yaml,
# web/manifest.json), and a blanket rule makes every one of them show as
# modified. Renormalizing those is a separate, explicit decision.

# Generated contracts and signed content must have deterministic bytes on Windows.
*.dart text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Never rewrite binary assets: golden snapshots, audio, images, fonts and Rive
# files are compared or hashed as exact bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.aac binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ogg binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.riv binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
